rs_ctrl_api_p2a2c.diff - phase 2a-2-C's header request (impl/notes_p2a2.md "2a-2-C", step 2: the pair's path marker).
The envelope's reserved 16 bytes get their name (pathMark: the RECORD's struct gdakiCtrlPathMark; gdakiCtrlEnvCheck
still does not read them), and the socket path's marker record GDAKI_TS_CTRL_PATH (56) with the marker struct and its
constants. Until it is merged the host file keeps the header blocks byte for byte (`api`) and has the same definitions
in its region "gin-control (ring): model" (the marker), writing the envelope's bytes at offsetof(struct gdakiCtrlEnv,
rsv); the merge drops the host's copies and renames rsv to pathMark there (one line).
Step 3 (impl/notes_p2a2.md "2a-2-C", the REJOIN over UD), appended: comments only. The nrp's generation rule
((incarnation << 20) + 1 for both kinds), the REJOIN_ACK's UD endpoint and the answers over UD (GDAKI_CTRL_RJA_*), and
what fd -1 means for the seams gdakiCtrlRecvOn and gdakiCtrlChanInstall (the REJOIN went over UD). The host file keeps
the header blocks byte for byte (`api`); the merge takes these comment lines into both.
Step 5 (impl/notes_p2a2.md "2a-2-C", STATE and the rkey list over the outbox; work step 3), appended: comments only.
The way of a pair's STATE turn (the REJOIN's, both sides; "not yet" until the pair is up in the REJOIN's generation; the data
socket only without a ring for the pair) beside the transfer head, and GDAKI_CTRL_CH_DATA's rdma meaning. The host
file keeps the header blocks byte for byte (`api`); the merge takes these comment lines into both.
